messages:
maria: Starting a config-only rollout for inference-proxy: applying safety limiter + token-throttle changes to reduce microburst CPU spikes. Plan = staggered rollout 20% -> 50% -> 100% with holds (20m, 30m). Kickoff now unless objections.

deploy-bot: config-only canary started · id=cfg-canary-2259876543 · service=inference-proxy · phase=20% · policy=staggered
Observability: https://console.redwood.internal/canary/cfg-canary-2259876543
Rollout plan: hold 20m, then 50%, then finalize to 100% after checks. Automated alerts wired to #eng-oncall.

olivia: Quick alignment: pin model_variant=prod-v3.1 for this canary (don't let autoswitch pick experimental quantized variants). Also set routing.policy=prefer-local for EU to avoid cross-region tails. Config snippet I'm applying: 
```json
{
  "safety_limiter": {
    "max_inflight_per_worker": 12,
    "token_throttle": {
      "burst_tokens": 6,
      "sustained_tps": 110
    }
  },
  "routing": {
    "policy": "prefer-local",
    "pin_model_variant": "prod-v3.1"
  },
  "batching": {
    "max_batch_size": 32,
    "tail_window_ms": 18
  }
}
```
Applied via config service; should be live in the canary bucket.

raj: Test thresholds to trigger rollback: if 95p latency increases by >200ms vs baseline OR error rate >0.4% (5xx + client errors combined) OR tokens/sec drops >8% -> immediate rollback. Also watch request distribution to ensure canary traffic isn't skewed (check route weights). I set a temporary alert: canary-latency-95p, canary-error-rate.

dave: I'll monitor traces and KV cache misses for the first 20m. If KV misses spike, we should pause and increase kv_warmup_seconds. Suggest kv_warmup_seconds = 45 for this change. Command to pause if needed: `rkctl canary pause cfg-canary-2259876543`

deploy-bot: advanced to 50% at 2259876663 · id=cfg-canary-2259876543 · phase=50% · note=No regressions observed in first hold window. Dashboard: https://console.redwood.internal/canary/cfg-canary-2259876543/overview

maria: Thanks team. Escalation path: if any alert defined by raj fires, ops will rollback to last pinned config and alert #incidents and the oncall rotation. Otherwise we'll complete to 100% at +1h and then remove the canary object. I'll post release notes after finalize.
